---
import PageLayout from '@/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
import EmailLink from '@/components/EmailLink.astro';
import { buildMeta } from '@/utils/seo';
import { getSiteSettings } from '@/utils/reader';

const site = await getSiteSettings();

const meta = buildMeta({
  title: 'Refund Policy',
  description: 'Refund policy for Panun Kaergar home services in Kashmir.',
  path: '/refund',
});
---

<PageLayout meta={meta}>
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900 sm:text-5xl">Refund Policy</h1>
    <div class="prose prose-slate mt-8 max-w-none">
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar manages the customer-facing side of every booking — acquisition, booking,
      pricing, communication, coordination, payment collection, support, feedback, and complaint
      handling. Independent service partners perform the work on site, but your booking and payment
      relationship is with Panun Kaergar.
    </p>
    <p>
      This page explains when you are eligible for a refund, how much may be refunded, and what
      happens after a partner visit, a cancellation, incomplete service, or a quality or damage
      complaint.
    </p>
    <p>
      Refund decisions depend mainly on: (1) whether our partner has visited the service site,
      (2) whether you paid only the booking confirmation amount or the full booking amount in
      advance, (3) whether the service was completed as confirmed, and (4) the result of any
      verification if work quality, damage, or a dispute is reported.
    </p>

    <h2>1. Payments through Panun Kaergar</h2>
    <p>
      Pay only the amount confirmed by Panun Kaergar through our official app, website, phone,
      WhatsApp, or other designated channel. Panun Kaergar collects customer payments and coordinates
      settlement with service partners. Refunds, adjustments, and payment guarantees apply only to
      genuine bookings handled through the official Panun Kaergar process and the company-approved
      amount — not to any separate amount agreed or collected outside that process.
    </p>
    <p>
      If a partner asks you to pay a different amount, pay in cash outside the approved process, or
      cancel your booking to deal privately, contact Panun Kaergar immediately before making any
      payment.
    </p>

    <h2>2. When you cancel the service</h2>
    <p>
      If you cancel a booked service, refund eligibility depends on whether our partner has already
      visited the site. See our <a href="/cancellation">cancellation policy</a> for how to cancel or
      reschedule.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If the service is cancelled by you after our partner has visited the site, the booking
      confirmation amount is not refundable. This amount covers the partner’s visit and related
      booking confirmation costs and will be retained.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has not visited the site</h3>
    <p>
      If the service is cancelled by you and our partner has not visited the site, the amount paid
      for the booking will be refunded. You are eligible for a full refund of what you have paid
      toward that booking (subject to verification of payment and booking status).
    </p>

    <h2>3. When you have paid the full booking amount in advance</h2>
    <p>
      Sometimes customers pay the full booking amount in advance rather than only the booking
      confirmation amount. In those cases, the refund works as follows:
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has only visited</h3>
    <p>
      If you have paid the full booking amount in advance and the partner has only visited the site
      (for example, the visit happened but the full service was not completed as booked, or you
      cancel after the visit), only the booking confirmation amount will be deducted. The remaining
      balance of the full amount you paid in advance will be refunded to you.
    </p>
    <h3>Partner has not visited</h3>
    <p>
      If you have paid the full booking amount in advance and the partner has not visited the site,
      the entire amount paid will be refunded. No booking confirmation deduction applies when the
      partner has not visited.
    </p>

    <h2>4. When Panun Kaergar cancels or cannot complete the visit</h2>
    <p>
      If Panun Kaergar cancels a booking because a partner is unavailable, there is a no-show,
      operational constraints prevent the visit, or we cannot complete the service as confirmed, we
      will try to offer a suitable reschedule first.
    </p>
    <p>
      If no suitable reschedule is possible and the partner has not visited the site, amounts paid
      toward that booking will be refunded in full. If a partner has already visited and the
      remainder of the service cannot be completed for reasons on our side, we will apply a refund
      or adjustment based on what was delivered and the verified booking details.
    </p>

    <h2>5. Service not delivered or incomplete as confirmed</h2>
    <p>
      If the service was not delivered as confirmed in your booking, was left incomplete without
      reasonable explanation, or required rework because of poor workmanship, contact Panun Kaergar
      support. We will review the booking record, partner visit status, and any available evidence
      before deciding on a refund, partial refund, reschedule, or corrective rework.
    </p>

    <h2>6. Poor workmanship or damage caused by the partner</h2>
    <p>
      If the partner has not worked properly, or if something is damaged because of the partner’s
      work, raise a complaint with our support team. Panun Kaergar coordinates the review and may
      request reasonable evidence — such as photographs, job notes, or other booking records —
      before any refund or corrective action is approved.
    </p>
    <h3>After verification — fault is from our partner</h3>
    <p>
      If, after verification, we confirm that the poor workmanship or damage was caused by our
      partner, we will provide a refund, partial refund, or other remedy as applicable to your
      booking and the verified issue.
    </p>
    <h3>After verification — fault is not from our side</h3>
    <p>
      If, after verification, we find that the fault is not from our side (or our partner), we will
      not provide a refund. Refunds are only given when the issue is verified as related to our
      partner’s work or responsibility under the booking.
    </p>
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar may assist in resolving customer complaints, but service partners remain
      responsible for damage or injury caused by their negligence, improper workmanship, misconduct,
      or unauthorized actions on site.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Additional work, scope changes, and materials</h2>
    <p>
      Panun Kaergar confirms the customer-facing price for each booking. If additional work, a
      change in scope, or extra materials are needed during the visit, contact Panun Kaergar before
      any extra amount is agreed or paid. Amounts paid or agreed outside the official Panun Kaergar
      process are not covered by this refund policy.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Other cases where a refund may apply</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>
        We are unable to complete the visit and cannot offer a suitable reschedule for your booking.
      </li>
      <li>Duplicate or erroneous charges, after verification by our support team.</li>
      <li>
        A verified overpayment relative to the company-approved booking amount, after review of the
        booking and payment records.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>9. Summary</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You cancel + partner has visited → booking confirmation amount is not refundable.</li>
      <li>You cancel + partner has not visited → amount paid is refunded.</li>
      <li>
        Full amount paid in advance + partner has only visited → booking confirmation amount
        deducted; remaining amount refunded.
      </li>
      <li>Full amount paid in advance + partner has not visited → full amount refunded.</li>
      <li>
        Panun Kaergar cancels before a partner visit and no suitable reschedule → full refund of
        amounts paid.
      </li>
      <li>Service not delivered or incomplete as confirmed → review and refund or remedy as applicable.</li>
      <li>Poor work or damage verified as caused by the partner → refund or remedy as applicable.</li>
      <li>After verification, fault is not from our side → no refund.</li>
      <li>Payments made outside the official Panun Kaergar process → not covered by this policy.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>10. How to request a refund</h2>
    <p>
      To request a refund or raise a service complaint, contact Panun Kaergar with your booking
      details (booking reference, service date, and a short description of the issue) by phone at
      <a href={`tel:${site.phone}`}>{site.phone}</a>, WhatsApp, or email at
      <EmailLink email={site.email} />. Our team will review your case, verify partner visit status
      and any quality, damage, or payment claim where needed, and respond as soon as possible.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Processing time</h2>
    <p>
      Approved refunds are processed to your original payment method where applicable. The time it
      takes for the amount to reflect in your account may vary depending on your bank or payment
      provider.
    </p>
    <p>
      For cancellation steps, see our <a href="/cancellation">cancellation policy</a>. For help with
      a specific booking, <a href="/contact">contact support</a>.
    </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</PageLayout>
